# Cost fixture for `just rooting-cost-gate` -- see scripts/rooting_cost_gate.sh.
#
# The THIRD size.  Its siblings (60 and 120) give one per-element figure; this one
# gives a second, at double the block length, and the gate compares them.  A cost
# that is quadratic in block length doubles between the two while a linear one
# holds flat, so the comparison sees the SHAPE rather than the level.
#
# That distinction is not academic here: a per-element arena-byte ceiling of
# 550000 stayed green while the real cost per element was 397637 and rising with
# every element added, because one measurement cannot tell a big constant from a
# growing one.
#
# Same shape as the other two, element for element.  Change one, change all three.

fn rows() -> List String =
  [
    int_to_string(0) ++ "-row",
    int_to_string(1) ++ "-row",
    int_to_string(2) ++ "-row",
